*** After the 2!d waiting response

Opener rebids 2NT with 22--24 HCP balanced (or with no five-card suit, such as
4-4-4-1, since 2!c is forcing and there is no better call), and 3NT with 25+ and
no five-card suit (NOTES.md #C8), using the same Stayman and
Jacoby-transfer structure as a 2NT opening (responder's ranges shifted for the
stronger 22--24 opener: game from 3 hcp, the quantitative 4NT at 9--10, 6NT at
11+). A suit rebid is forcing to 3 of opener's major or 4 of opener's minor:
responder raises with three-card support, shows a five-card suit of his own
with 8+ hcp, and otherwise makes the waiting 2NT (after a major) or 3NT (after
a minor) rather than passing a forcing bid.

