A raise of responder's suit after a 2/1-style continuation is not automatically
forcing to game; for example, after 2!c-2!d-2!h-2!s, a 3!h rebid is a non-forcing
preference.

2C-2D-2H-2S-
3S = 3+!s
2N = bal
3H = NF, unlimited

** Interference over 2!c

If an opponent overcalls 2!c, responder passes with a weak hand (0--7) and
doubles with values (8+); if an opponent doubles, responder redoubles with
values and otherwise passes. If an opponent overcalls the 2!d waiting response,
opener doubles for penalty with length in their suit, bids a five-card suit of
his own, or bids notrump (NOTES.md "Notrump lane" #N4).

